{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1pj:000040:note_appended:sase-1pj.1:739bc287023618da53bd3332d212ea0e557a2a6fa3be311ef0dff2feb58a3fdc","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:38:42Z","actor":"sase-1pj.1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-1pj.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP: Align core-memory authorization for staged handoffs — the approved plan requests the memory-sase.template.md final-declaration rewrite and regeneration, but memory_final_exemption authorizes macros.md only and the phase prompt forbids any other memory note. The child plan will update authorized macros.md and skills; the ancestor land agent should resolve authorization for the generated sase.md core-note change before docs-memory."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1pj:000041:note_appended:sase-1pj.1:9cd3019ae306415e771957a84968c13807664dbab02bc1385f8cc974c63d72d6","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:39:15Z","actor":"sase-1pj.1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-1pj.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP: Define staged-plan semantics for PR-mode projects — the approved epic excludes projects whose commit finalizer opens a PR, because successor phase agents cannot consume the pending commit; preserve this boundary and let the ancestor land agent triage it."}}
