{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1pj:000046:note_appended:sase-1pj.1:e879506fb9d601c36a9fafa92fcfa21256b9e92daae93cbfddd6f03744981b82","timestamp":"2026-10-29T08:57:49Z","actor":"sase-1pj.1.1.land","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-1pj.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"HANDOFF API (recorded by sase-1pj.1.1.land for handoff-wire, questions-pipe, gate-staging, monitor-staging, adoption-recovery): flag staged_handoffs is beta, default off, flag bead sase-1pk. Rust contract: sase-core crates/sase_core/src/staged_handoff (cd62c83d; stranded ownership 751bba5f), pinned in sase-core-revision.txt. Python facade sase.core.staged_handoff (validate_staged_handoff, validate_staged_handoff_receipt, evaluate_stage_admission, receipt_authorizes). Host API sase.agent.staged_handoff: staged_handoffs_enabled, acquire_staging_reservation/release_staging_reservation (take the reservation before side effects), write_staged_handoff (admission + reservation swap under the handoff then declaration lock), read_staged_handoff, discard_staged_handoff, read/write_adoption_receipt, receipt_authorizes, write/read_staged_handoff_response, occupying_handoff_names, admit_stage, and build_plan_staged_record (add a build_<kind>_staged_record per kind). Adoption: sase.axe.run_agent_exec_staged.STAGED_HANDOFF_ADOPTERS (kind -> adopter(staged_record, run_metadata, StagedInlineContinuation, response)), with only plan registered; dispatch_completed_staged_handoff runs after finalizer settlement and holds unsupported kinds with handoff_not_adopted. Legacy handoff_guard and write_pending_handoff_marker now share admission, so a legacy handoff after an accepted current /sase_final submission is also refused (protective: the kill path would otherwise skip the declared commit)."}}
